1
00:00:04,872 --> 00:00:07,412
(Penny:)-What are you working on?
-Can't talk. In the zone.

2
00:00:08,375 --> 00:00:10,215
(Penny:)-Do you know what he's doing?
-Could be anything.

3
00:00:10,377 --> 00:00:11,857
(Amy:)Last time he was like this,
he figured out

4
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:13,822
(Amy:)electron transport in graphene.

5
00:00:13,981 --> 00:00:15,861
(Amy:)The time before that,
he was making a list of who's allowed

6
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,186
in his tree fort if he ever gets ons.

7
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:21,333
(Amy:)Still can't believe
I didn't make the cut.

8
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,500
(Penny:)Sheldon, you want to take a break?
Your food's ready.

9
00:00:25,659 --> 00:00:28,939
(Leonard:)No, what are you doing?
He's both happy and quiet.

10
00:00:29,096 --> 00:00:32,076
(Leonard:)It's like seeing a unicorn
and Bigfoot at the same time.

11
00:00:33,934 --> 00:00:35,204
(Howard:)Sorry we're so late.

12
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:37,009
(Howard:)Bernadette got stuck at work.

13
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:40,280
Great news! A raccoon virus
just crossed the species barrier

14
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:42,940
and now can infect humans!

15
00:00:44,011 --> 00:00:45,351
(Raj:)Why is that great news?

16
00:00:45,512 --> 00:00:47,462
(Bernadette:)In the pharmaceutical business,

17
00:00:47,614 --> 00:00:48,884
"Mo' infections, mo' money."

18
00:00:50,617 --> 00:00:52,097
Wait!

19
00:00:52,252 --> 00:00:54,592
(Howard:)Maybe you want to wash
your little raccoon hands first.

20
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:57,365
(Bernadette:)Calm down.
If I had it, I'd be dead already.

21
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,460
(Howard:)Guys, listen up.

22
00:01:01,628 --> 00:01:02,698
(Sheldon:)Can't listen, zone.

23
00:01:03,864 --> 00:01:05,464
(Sheldon:)Also don't care.

24
00:01:06,466 --> 00:01:08,776
(Howard:)Next week is the anniversary
of my first date with Bernadette.

25
00:01:08,936 --> 00:01:10,976
(Sheldon:)Really don't care.

26
00:01:11,138 --> 00:01:12,478
(Howard:)I want to do something special,

27
00:01:12,639 --> 00:01:14,309
(Howard:)and I was hoping you guys
could be a part of it.

28
00:01:14,474 --> 00:01:17,454
(Penny:)What horrible thing
are you trying to make up for?

29
00:01:17,611 --> 00:01:20,591
(Howard:)Just putting something in the bank
for what horrible thing I do next.

30
00:01:20,714 --> 00:01:21,424
(Penny:)Ah.

31
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:25,130
Lock, she's gonna be back any second,

32
00:01:25,285 --> 00:01:27,825
I'm writing a song, and hoping we
could all play it for her together.

33
00:01:27,988 --> 00:01:30,058
(Amy:)-I love that.
-That is so beautiful.

34
00:01:30,223 --> 00:01:31,563
(Howard:)Sheldon?

35
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,000
(Sheldon:)When did we get
to The Cheesecake Factory?

36
00:01:36,496 --> 00:01:38,976
I (THEME SONG PLAYS) I

